Advanced motor-driven service and repair study (@pe-motor-study: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR", #source "../sources/Motor-Rewind-Study-and-Good-Practice-EASA-AEMT.lingua#r_3K38XSH8DWC79G20NF55ATKEJP", #source "../sources/Electric-Machines-MIT-6-685.lingua#r_6A4HM4XV13NAZDRV92PZDJ31XH", #source "../sources/Power-Electronics-MIT-6-334.lingua#r_071M46GNC27PPJVTZEQTMEF526", #electrical-power-engineering "../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3") { r_5ZRD36TPD8KGSV0DBSW229N2EG
**Read:** [Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE](../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR), entire sourcebook; [Motor rewind studies and good practice — EASA/AEMT](../sources/Motor-Rewind-Study-and-Good-Practice-EASA-AEMT.lingua#r_3K38XSH8DWC79G20NF55ATKEJP), both entire studies and the full authorized practice guide; [Electric Machines — MIT 6.685, Fall 2013](../sources/Electric-Machines-MIT-6-685.lingua#r_6A4HM4XV13NAZDRV92PZDJ31XH), complete applicable design/dynamic/control chapters; [Power Electronics — MIT 6.334, Spring 2007](../sources/Power-Electronics-MIT-6-334.lingua#r_071M46GNC27PPJVTZEQTMEF526), whole applicable drive/converter methods.

Read all of [Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE](../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR), the complete machine/drive development from [Electric Machines — MIT 6.685, Fall 2013](../sources/Electric-Machines-MIT-6-685.lingua#r_6A4HM4XV13NAZDRV92PZDJ31XH) and [Power Electronics — MIT 6.334, Spring 2007](../sources/Power-Electronics-MIT-6-334.lingua#r_071M46GNC27PPJVTZEQTMEF526), and both entire [Motor rewind studies and good practice — EASA/AEMT](../sources/Motor-Rewind-Study-and-Good-Practice-EASA-AEMT.lingua#r_3K38XSH8DWC79G20NF55ATKEJP) studies with the separate authorized good-practice method. Choose a documented pump, fan or process drive with an actual torque/speed/duty requirement.

Derive electrical, electromagnetic, mechanical and thermal models sufficient for startup and steady/variable operation. Compare direct, reduced-voltage and controlled operation with network voltage/current, protection, energy and useful service. Distinguish machine efficiency, drive efficiency and process performance. Use actual tests/material/condition evidence rather than only nominal ratings.

Investigate repair/rewind versus replacement or a changed control strategy. Trace winding/core preparation, conductor resistance, bearings, cooling and material compatibility to measurable losses and condition. Predict a changed operating point independently and quantify uncertainty. Appropriate supervised workshop/testing can establish practical capability; an authorized full case reconstruction supplies different evidence. Finish with a defended service decision, its limitations and what must be maintained or rechecked after the intervention.

**Continue:** [An integrated electrical-power-system investigation](../study/An-integrated-electrical-power-system-investigation.lingua#r_06BN864FF9C0AN3EWZJE78Y6Y3).

**Return:** [Electrical power engineering — sources, networks, machines and continuing service](../Electrical-power-engineering.lingua#r_300EPNGATK7PHWNZCQFBXGZFCQ).
